# width: 120
# height: 40
# The tab strip's ` +N hidden ` chip paints whenever ANY tab is off the
# strip — not only when the strip happens to be scrolled to a tail that
# fits whole. The chip used to be painted after the last chip with
# whatever room was left before the chevrons, and in the ordinary
# overflow case (the last chip cut at the right edge) there was none,
# so twelve buffers at 120 columns said nothing about the missing ones.
# `stripRight` decides the chips' right edge before anything is painted:
# the chip takes the leftover cells where there are some (a whole tail
# lays out exactly as before), and is GIVEN cells where there are not.
write file01name.txt x
write file02name.txt x
write file03name.txt x
write file04name.txt x
write file05name.txt x
write file06name.txt x
write file07name.txt x
write file08name.txt x
write file09name.txt x
write file10name.txt x
write file11name.txt x
write file12name.txt x
open file01name.txt
open file02name.txt
open file03name.txt
open file04name.txt
open file05name.txt
open file06name.txt
open file07name.txt
open file08name.txt
open file09name.txt
open file10name.txt
open file11name.txt
open file12name.txt
expect screen contains "file12name.txt"
expect screen contains " hidden "
